# Copy to .env.local. This deployment needs three variables, and that is the
# whole list — no Supabase keys, no OpenAI key, no Stripe or Razorpay secrets.
#
# SPLIT 2026-09-01: that shortness is the point, not an oversight. This site
# asks nobody whether they are signed in and starts no checkout; it links to the
# app, which does both. So it holds no credentials, and the blast radius of a
# marketing deploy is a marketing deploy.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── origins

# The product app — auth, dashboard, admin and every /api route. Every "Log in",
# "Get started", Buy button and download link on this site is built from it; see
# lib/app-links.js.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is required, not stylistic: PricingPlans is a client component and
# reads this in the browser, so it must be inlined at build time. Without the
# prefix every Buy button navigates to "undefined/dashboard/billing".
#
# 127.0.0.1 rather than localhost, to match apps/desktop/.env — one spelling of
# "the local app" across the repo.
#
# SET THIS AT BUILD TIME, NOT ONLY AT RUNTIME. /features and /how-it-works are
# statically prerendered, so they bake whatever was in the environment during
# `next build` straight into their HTML. / and /pricing are dynamic and read it
# per request. A deployment that injects this only at runtime therefore ships
# two of five pages pointing at localhost while the other three look fine — and
# nothing errors. See the long note in lib/app-links.js.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000

# This site's own origin. Feeds metadataBase in app/layout.js, plus sitemap.js
# and robots.js. Without it, canonical and openGraph URLs resolve against the
# deployment hostname — which on a preview means preview URLs in production tags.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3002

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── payments

# NOT A CREDENTIAL. It is a plain boolean, and it exists so that /compare can
# say whether UPI is live without this deployment holding RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET
# just to answer one row of a table. See razorpayLive() in
# packages/pricing/src/gateway.js for the full reasoning and the drift it costs.
#
# Set it to true only when the Razorpay keys are actually set on the APP
# deployment. If the two disagree, /compare claims UPI is available while
# checkout quietly falls back to Stripe.
RAZORPAY_LIVE=false
